{"abstract":[{"text":"A least-cost flow meeting every supply (positive: the vertex sends that much more than it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"receives; negative: a demand), within capacities (LEMON ","type":"text"},{"code":"NetworkSimplex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", OR-Tools","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"SimpleMinCostFlow","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", NetworkX ","type":"text"},{"code":"min_cost_flow","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with the opposite sign), or nil when there is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"none: the supplies do not sum to zero, or some set of vertices supplies more than its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out-edges carry. Costs may be negative; negative cycles are saturated (capacities are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"finite). A self-loop carries its capacity when its cost is negative and nothing otherwise.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Network simplex with block-search pivots and strongly feasible trees, LEMON’s layout.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"supply","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called once per vertex in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order, then, for each edge in position","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order, ","type":"text"},{"code":"capacity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and then ","type":"text"},{"code":"cost","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", before any work. Which optimum is returned when several","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exist is unspecified, but the same input always gives the same result.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumCostFlow"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":", 